  "discussion": {
    "headline": "Poor Air Quality Today followed by severe storms on saturday",
    "dateLine": "3:00 p.m. Friday, July 17, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "The third heatwave of the year scorched the mid-Atlantic States this week, but its intensity and duration both paled in comparison to the early-July scorcher. However, high temperatures still reached the mid 90s in most spots on Wednesday and Thursday, and maximum heat indices topped out between 100-105°F both afternoons. Wednesday's high of 96°F at Millersville University ultimately came up 4°F short of tying the July 15th record high of 100°F from 1997 (see below). …",
